    <h2 id="report">Report a vulnerability</h2>
    <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:security@getcmdr.com">security@getcmdr.com</a>, or use GitHub's private reporting (the
        <a href="https://github.com/vdavid/cmdr/security/advisories/new">Report a vulnerability</a> button on the
        repository's Security tab). There's no PGP key, by choice: send details you'd rather not email through GitHub's
        private reporting. Please don't open a public GitHub issue. The full policy, including scope and safe harbor, is
        <a href="https://github.com/vdavid/cmdr/blob/main/SECURITY.md">SECURITY.md</a> on GitHub, also linked from
        <a href="/.well-known/security.txt">security.txt</a>. Only the latest version gets fixes. What to expect:
    </p>
    <ul>
        {vulnerabilityResponse.map((line) => <li>{line}</li>)}
    </ul>
    <DevTodo>
        If you change the response times, change them in <code>SECURITY.md</code> too.
    </DevTodo>

    <h2 id="gaps">Not in place yet</h2>
    <p>These are the gaps a careful review would find. They're listed here so you don't have to look for them.</p>
    <ul>
        {notInPlaceYet.map((gap) => <li set:html={gap} />)}
    </ul>
    <DevTodo>
        Bars a security team may still expect that this page can't claim: a signed DPA, a protected release
        environment for the signing secrets (they're
        plain repo secrets today, with no branch protection), and a continuity clause. Each one you add moves a line
        out of this list.
    </DevTodo>
</LegalLayout>
